     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m currently trying to estimate the number of fixed differences between 7 populations of a &#39;species&#39; (including probably cryptic species). However, nearly all populations have only <i>n = </i>4 (one has 3, another has 2) so the command &#39;gl.fixed.diff&#39; won&#39;t run as <i>n</i>&lt;5. The documentation mentions that this can be changed &quot;using the parameter nlimit&quot;, but I&#39;m not exactly sure how to add this to the command? It doesn&#39;t seem to be an option within &#39;gl.fixed.diff&#39;?</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve had some issues with input file formatting that I&#39;m working on, but if anyone could clarify how to use this setting, that would be great.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers.</div><div>Sean Buckley</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
